# (0.15) Pop-up menus on the Desktop and in Files (DESK=1; tests/mousegen.py makes
# tests/desk15.keys from this; the card gets /GAME.ATR). Files is at (24, 24); its rows:
# GAME.ATR y 158, README.TXT 182. Shots (s):
#   1   6.0  a right click on the Atari icon: its menu (nothing loaded: Eject all dimmed)
#   2   8.5  Attach disk...: the file dialog lists only folders and disk images; "g" typed:
#            GAME.ATR selected (type-ahead), its name in the field
#   3  11.5  Enter: GAME.ATR on D1: (the icon's mark); the Atari menu again: "Eject D1: GAME.ATR"
#   4  14.0  that Eject chosen; a right click on README.TXT in Files: Open, Open with Edit,
#            Open with Write, -, Copy, Add to desktop, -, Rename..., Delete
#   5  16.8  Esc; GAME.ATR's menu: Load into Atari: D1: in Files' footer
#   6  18.3  a right click below the rows: New folder..., Paste (dimmed), -, Parent folder
#            (dimmed at the root)
#   7  20.5  New folder...: the name dialog; a right click in its field: Cut, Copy, Paste
#            (dimmed), -, Select all
#   8  24.0  Esc, Esc; the desktop's menu (above the pointer): New folder..., Tidy up, -,
#            Settings...
#   9  27.5  New folder..., Enter: the folder "New folder" in /Desktop (its icon); its menu
#  10  31.0  Rename...: "Games" typed, Enter: the icon renamed
#  11  35.0  README.TXT > Open with Edit; a right click in its text: Undo, Redo, -, Cut,
#            Copy, Paste, Select all
#  12  38.0  Esc; the menu key in Edit: the same menu at the top left of the text (from the
#            keyboard: its first item highlighted)
